# Secrets

- Read secrets only from environment variables: for cloud agents, set in the
  Cursor dashboard (Cloud Agents > Secrets); in CI, GitHub Actions secrets;
  locally, `.env`, which git ignores. `.env.example` lists each one by name,
  with no value; add the name in the PR that first reads it.
- Never commit a secret or write one to a log, error message, test, PR, or
  issue; name its variable instead. Don't print the environment (`env`) or
  trace commands that use one (`set -x`).
- If a secret you need is missing, stop and name the variable a person must
  set. Never hard-code its value or a default for it.
- If a secret was committed or logged, tell a person at once so they can
  revoke it; deleting it afterwards doesn't undo the leak.
